Launch an actual terminal child; verify it sees a terminal, initial dimensions, resizing, literal input, unread draining, final output and nonzero exit.
Run an interactive system shell and verify arithmetic output and clean exit.
Connect subprocesses carrying 2.5 MiB of binary data; verify byte count and checksum, and exact file redirection beyond capture limits.
Verify pipeline input, ordered stage exits, upstream failure status, stderr, failed first stage and cleanup when a later stage cannot launch.
Verify session PATH, HOME and paths containing spaces in command/path completion; retain embedded apostrophes in CLI quoted completion.
Verify terminal byte readers remain independent across split Unicode characters, ring truncation and bounded cursor batches.
Wait on live terminal and pipeline objects while querying status and inspector views, then stop them through their control mailbox.
